# `true`/`false` are NOT keywords/boolean literals in EigenScript — the C VM has
# no such tokens, so they are ordinary identifiers (EigenScript uses 1/0). The
# front-end used to lex them into literal 1/0, which silently miscompiled
# `print of true` to `1` and rejected `true is 5`. They must behave as plain
# names here, byte-for-byte with the C evaluator.
true is 5
false is 7
print of (true + false)
print of true
local truthy is 1
print of truthy
